WEBVTT

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:46.270
The pest control guys have my office building completely sealed off.

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:48.230
I'm gonna have to work from home the next week.

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:49.990
Whoa, you seeing patients in your house?

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:52.950
Only in case of emergency. I'm pretty much on standby.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:56.400
I'll just use the time to catch up on the latest psychiatric journals.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.320
Fun.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:59.330
You ever considered taking a holiday?

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:00.000
Actually,

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:04.610
Sabrina just booked a beach vacation, but I just get so bored laying around all the time.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:05.590
You? No.

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:08.490
Whoa, Kurt.

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:10.700
So great to see you.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:11.480
You too.

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:13.210
What are you doing in Atlanta?

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:14.850
I transferred to the base in Albany.

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:17.610
I'm in logistics, and my wife Kayla's here now.

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:19.110
Oh, so sorry.

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:21.010
Kurt, this is my friend Haley.

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:25.310
Kurt and I served together in the Marine Corps, and Haley and I served together in the VA's office.

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:26.150
Nice to meet you.

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:26.590
Likewise.

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:29.060
Oh, excuse me.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:36.200
Everything okay?

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.200
Not the call I was open for.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.200
How long are you in town?

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:39.200
Were you here for the day?

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.200
What's going on?

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.200
I'm here half the week.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.200
I'm on base the other half.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:43.200
I'm in charge of the contractors out of Atlanta.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.200
So I'm doing the inspection, arrange a transpo, that kind of thing.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:50.200
Not exactly like patrolling a stretch of desert littered with IEDs now, is it?

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:54.390
Not exactly, but just as dangerous.

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:58.990
You know, we're all going out to dinner tomorrow night.

00:01:58.990 --> 00:01:59.990
You and your wife should come out.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:00.900
Come along with us.

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:01.720
- Yeah.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:02.560
- Yeah, Kayla, we really like that.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:04.060
Yeah, she could use some friends in the city.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:06.500
- Great, you can tell me all about Fincher the Marine.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:09.600
- Only if you tell me all about Fincher the Investigator.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.280
- Do I get to join this conversation?

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:13.370
- We'll see.

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:14.350
- It was great to see you, man.

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:15.170
- My man.

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:16.010
- All right.

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:16.760
- Nice meeting you.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:22.260
- So one night we were out on patrol

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.460
and I found a dead camel spider.

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:25.730
And I don't know if you've ever seen them,

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:26.830
but they're pretty big.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:27.670
- Pretty big?

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:28.710
Just as big as my hand.

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:30.000
- Okay.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.380
When you went to sleep, I slipped one in his boot and I got woken up to the loudest scream

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:38.460
I've ever heard in my entire life.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.460
That is just like med school.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:41.460
I don't know.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:42.280
Tell him why.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:46.300
It turns out his spider wasn't dead.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.160
Now I know why you're afraid of spiders.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:50.360
Yes, I'm just scarred to this day.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:52.930
Get that away.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:54.930
You don't need to check your phone every three seconds.

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:56.070
Sorry.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:57.070
I'm just expecting a call.

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:59.250
You're always expecting a call.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:00.760
- Hmm.

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:04.420
- So, Kurt, how is it that you've been based in Atlanta?

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:05.980
Are you a recruiter?

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:08.180
- No, I'm posted to the base in Albany.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:11.000
But my job is to liaise with the civilian contractors

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.360
based here in Atlanta.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:14.720
So I'm here half a week and I'm based the other day.

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:16.400
- Kayla gets to live in a regular city again

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:17.700
like a normal civilian.

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:18.980
I get to spend a lot of time with her.

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:20.520
- And there's no camel spiders here, so.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:21.620
- Yes. - None.

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:24.180
- Where's the ladies room?

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:25.380
- Oh, I've seen that.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:27.790
Thank you.

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:30.000
- Kurt, I have the same fitness tracker

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.240
and I love it.

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:33.410
- Oh, Kayla bought it for me.

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:35.410
Honestly, I don't even know how to work the thing.

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:37.810
I wear it for her, but really I just use it as a watch.

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:39.570
- I noticed a huge difference in my workouts.

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:41.570
I can show you how to use it if you'd like.

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:44.570
- Might take you up on that sometime.

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:48.850
Excuse me, I need to make a call.

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:53.710
- Maybe you should go check up on me.

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:55.070
- Oh, you may not know this,

00:03:55.070 --> 00:03:57.820
but I was recently made chair of the fundraising committee

00:03:57.820 --> 00:03:58.720
at Atlanta Memorial.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:00.000
- Congratulations, Megan.

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:05.590
thank you i'm very excited so i put together a calendar featuring men of the hospital it's a

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:11.990
great idea i thought so but i've hit a bit of a snag so it's sitting at the printers about to be

00:04:11.990 --> 00:04:17.450
assembled and shipped off but one of my models had a change of heart and he won't sign the release so

00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:30.000
i'm without a mr november and unless i find one the whole project is sunk are you asking me to do it i know you

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.480
for the city coroner which means you don't technically work for the hospital but you

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:43.010
you work with us all the time and i'm desperate jonas i can't find anyone and if things fall

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:50.260
apart i will have blown our budget for the year with nothing to show for it i i don't know just

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:57.090
think about it but get back to me by tomorrow okay oh okay no pressure i think i need another drink

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:00.000
what's going on with you and kayla

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.080
We're just trying to adjust to all this.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:07.290
I've been a bit preoccupied lately.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:08.440
Yeah.

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:11.010
You get in touch with whoever's got you so worried?

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:13.420
I'm not so good at the set of huge, am I?

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:13.900
Mm-mm.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:15.060
Never were.

00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:17.190
Wanna talk about it?

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:22.360
It's not the right time.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:23.720
Whenever.

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:25.960
It's no expiration date on my offer.

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:27.190
Thanks.

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:29.130
I take you up on that.

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:29.730
Just...

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:32.920
Not yet.

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:35.440
Here you are.

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:36.600
What happened?

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.500
I just have a headache.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:40.810
I'm going home.

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:41.850
You can stay if you want.

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:43.050
No, no, let's go.

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:45.960
Um, give my excuses to everyone, will you?

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:46.790
Of course.

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:48.230
It's nice to see you, Venture.

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:49.010
You too.

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:51.180
Call me, okay?

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:51.940
I mean it.

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:52.530
No, what?

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:09.560
you're quiet am i going too fast for you no i've just been thinking about what megan was asking me

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:17.150
last night oh the calendar yeah i mean i know how expensive it is for hospitals to stay current and

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:21.560
fundraising is essential true but i just don't think i'm the kind of person who likes to be

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:28.870
the center of attention you're the center of my attention my favorite place to be what do you think

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:34.760
It's good for the hospital, it's good for you to do something you don't normally do.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:37.160
Besides, I wouldn't mind dating a model.

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:39.960
A medical examiner doesn't do it for you?

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:43.250
Why can't I have both?

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:45.750
I guess at the very least I can guarantee them one sale.

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:46.630
Two.

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:47.630
I'll need one for my office.

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:50.260
All right then, I'll do it.

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:51.030
Okay.

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:53.700
We're gonna have to pick up the pace, you're gonna need to be in shape if you're gonna

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:54.700
be all famous.

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:57.510
I'm hardly gonna be famous, it's just a hospital calendar.

00:06:57.510 --> 00:07:00.000
Stop making excuses because you're slow.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.100
- Oh, okay, it's on.

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:03.420
I'll race you to the last land park.

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:04.880
- Okay.

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:06.020
- Waiter buys breakfast.

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:14.540
- Oh, of course.

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:15.580
- I got you.

00:07:21.070 --> 00:07:23.160
Hey, Kurt, what's going on?

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:27.790
- Fincher, I think I need to take you up on your offer.

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:28.800
- Yeah, yeah, what's up?

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:32.460
- Not over the phone.

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:35.180
- Um, okay, well, I'm on a stakeout right now,

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:38.310
but I can swing by your place in about an hour.

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:39.290
- I have to head to base.

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:41.160
I'll be back in Atlanta on Sunday.

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:44.420
- Okay, um, Sunday.

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:47.010
Sunday's fine, we can meet up.

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:48.470
Kurt, you sure you're okay?

00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:52.420
- Yeah, maybe not.

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:54.980
We'll talk on Sunday.

00:07:54.980 --> 00:07:55.480
- Okay.

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:15.280
- Good job on the Brody case.

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:16.720
I think we might get a conviction

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:18.480
with that corroborating evidence you found.

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:20.080
- Oh, my pleasure, Ms. District Attorney.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:23.700
- You do not have to call me that, Fincher.

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:25.180
Paulina will be fine.

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:27.260
- I know, I just love that you won the election, that's all.

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:29.860
- Yeah, more than a year ago.

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:32.550
- Hey, by the way, have you seen Haley?

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:33.830
- Yeah, I see Haley all the time.

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:34.940
- How's she doing?

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:37.340
- Getting in trouble as per usual.

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:39.130
- I've been meaning to give her a call.

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:40.930
- You should, she would love to hear from you.

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:42.210
- I will do, see you later.

00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:43.240
- All right.

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:44.390
- Mr. Garland.

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:45.390
- Yes.

00:08:45.390 --> 00:08:46.780
- Sergeant Nesuit.

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:48.000
- How may I be of service?

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:50.380
- We're looking for Staff Sergeant Kurt Cullen.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:51.600
Have you been in contact with him?

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:54.600
- We spoke yesterday, but you already know that.

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:56.210
- What did you talk about?

00:08:56.210 --> 00:08:59.550
- We made plans to get together on Sunday.

00:08:59.550 --> 00:09:00.000
- Do you know it's Kurt?

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.890
current whereabouts? I assumed he was on base. Please call me immediately if you do hear from him.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:10.940
I will when you tell me exactly what this is all about. Staff Sergeant Cohen is in violation of

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:16.870
his terms of service. How so? He failed to report for duty this morning and is currently absent

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:22.860
without leave. He's AWOL? No way. If you do hear from him, please tell me. I can still keep him

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:28.890
from getting into too much trouble, but not for much longer. Thanks, sirs.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:40.760
Haley, are you free?

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:45.060
Yeah, I think I need your help with something.

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:50.010
I just can't believe he would do this to me, especially since I told him I'm not comfortable

00:09:50.010 --> 00:09:51.010
in this house sometimes.

00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:54.010
Are you having trouble being alone when he's on base?

00:09:54.010 --> 00:09:56.010
Kurt's been overseas for most of our marriage.

00:09:56.010 --> 00:09:58.450
I'm not afraid to be alone, but...

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:07.560
the past few days i've just just had this feeling what feeling i swear someone's been watching this

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:15.210
house well have you seen anybody no i'm sure it's just my mind playing tricks on me i've been angry

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:23.460
with kurt and i've just been on edge what's been troubling you nothing something to do with kurt

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:30.000
you have an idea of what's happening and i can see that you find it

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:36.860
deeply hurtful we're here to support you i just want to find kurt before the mps do help him with

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:41.020
whatever trouble he's in i don't know what's going on i don't know anything for sure what do you

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:54.370
suspect i think kurt's left me for another woman why would you think that he keeps secrets he

00:10:54.370 --> 00:11:00.000
pretends like he's at atlanta to spend time with me but when he's here i barely see him

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:07.710
him. How long has he been like this? A few weeks maybe. We've only been here four months. Kurt told

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:15.660
me the whole reason he took the transfer was for you. Yeah, maybe it was then, but things have

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:22.940
changed. I know it's hard, but try not to jump to conclusions. There may be another explanation.

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:26.940
We'll find him, Kayla. I promise.

00:11:31.150 --> 00:11:33.250
- I just can't believe that Kurt would run off on Kayla,

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:34.410
even if they were having problems.

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:35.730
I mean, he wouldn't do something like that.

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:38.380
- We all sensed the tension between them the other night.

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:39.840
- Yeah, but the other man I served with,

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:41.420
he wasn't a deserter or a cheater.

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:42.640
- People change Fincher.

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:45.300
You haven't known him for a while.

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:46.660
- Yeah, but you just don't get this, Haley.

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:47.480
You can't.

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:50.400
Serving in the military, it's like having another family.

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:52.740
You don't like everyone, you don't get along with everyone,

00:11:52.740 --> 00:11:54.420
but your brother's all the same.

00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:56.460
And you know them like no one else,

00:11:56.460 --> 00:11:59.620
not like their parents, not like their wives,

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:00.000
and I'm telling you,

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:03.030
I know Curt Cullen. He's not that kind of guy.

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:11.880
Sorry to ask for your help, Monty.

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:15.370
I know with Danny being away into Florida for his parents' anniversary, you must be swamped.

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:18.330
Oh, that's not it, Fincher. You know, I would love to help you out,

00:12:18.330 --> 00:12:22.330
but it's not our jurisdiction, and the military MPs have not asked for our help.

00:12:22.330 --> 00:12:24.070
Is there really nothing you can do?

00:12:24.070 --> 00:12:27.840
Look, I'm sure the MPs are doing everything that we would in this situation.

00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:30.000
I'm really sorry. My hands are tied.

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:32.660
- I understand.

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:34.430
- So now what?

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:35.510
- Well, he left his phone in home,

00:12:35.510 --> 00:12:36.730
so even if we could get into it,

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:39.030
it won't tell us where he is now.

00:12:39.030 --> 00:12:40.540
- What about his fitness tracker?

00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:43.340
He's the same one I had, it has GPS.

00:12:43.340 --> 00:12:44.800
- Well, how do we access it?

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:48.380
- Just log in.

00:12:48.380 --> 00:12:50.880
- Let's hope he didn't change his password.

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:53.200
- Caleb bought Kurt the fitness tracker

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:54.560
and he said he didn't know how to use it,

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:56.940
so my guess is he never even logged into his account,

00:12:56.940 --> 00:12:58.770
much less changed the default password.

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:03.530
And I'm in.

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:05.180
What can you see?

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:10.710
Well, the fitness tracker is not currently active, but that could just mean that he took it off.

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:13.270
Can you see the last time it was active?

00:13:13.740 --> 00:13:17.740
9 p.m. last night, but after that it goes dark, nothing else.

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:19.020
Where was he at 9 p.m.?

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:19.740
Still in Atlanta.

00:13:21.130 --> 00:13:21.770
That's odd.

00:13:22.100 --> 00:13:23.980
He should have been halfway back to Albany by that time.

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:25.680
Does it say exactly where?

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:26.590
It does.

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:28.670
The wooded area of Piercedale Park.

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:34.280
This is it.

00:13:34.280 --> 00:13:37.510
Let's go see what we can find.

00:13:37.510 --> 00:13:40.130
Are we in the right spot?

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:43.330
Well, the coordinates on the fitness tracker

00:13:43.330 --> 00:13:45.070
show it to be basically right here.

00:13:45.070 --> 00:13:47.120
If there's something to find, it's pretty close.

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:23.250
find anything on him. Anything in the surrounding area? Wallet? Keys?

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:26.170
Nothing. No idea on him at all. Could have been a robbery.

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:28.100
Why leave the fitness tracker?

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:29.480
True.

00:14:30.280 --> 00:14:33.790
