01:00:00.670 --> 01:00:03.060
- Where'd you get this photo?

01:00:03.060 --> 01:00:07.840
- Does it have a special significance to you?

01:00:07.840 --> 01:00:11.190
- No, I've never seen it before.

01:00:11.190 --> 01:00:14.660
- I'm sorry, Mr. Park, I know this is a lot to process,

01:00:14.660 --> 01:00:19.950
but we need to ask you some questions.

01:00:19.950 --> 01:00:24.920
Did you know Staff Sergeant Cullen?

01:00:24.920 --> 01:00:27.040
- No, not personally.

01:00:27.040 --> 01:00:29.060
- He moved outside of his house last week.

01:00:36.460 --> 01:00:37.600
Have you ever seen this before?

01:00:39.310 --> 01:00:40.210
No.

01:00:41.140 --> 01:00:42.850
So you weren't trying to get it back?

01:00:43.300 --> 01:00:43.660
No.

01:00:45.460 --> 01:00:47.620
Mr. Park, we found your fingerprints on it.

01:00:49.870 --> 01:00:52.510
I sent him the letter.

01:00:53.360 --> 01:00:55.340
But then I heard on the news that he was found dead.

01:00:56.040 --> 01:00:57.520
I knew what that was going to look like.

01:00:58.900 --> 01:01:00.000
But hey, I didn't kill him.

01:01:01.690 --> 01:01:04.360
I just wanted some justice for my daughter.

01:01:04.360 --> 01:01:09.350
And you think Kirk Cohn was responsible for what happened to her?

01:01:09.350 --> 01:01:13.530
I don't know.

01:01:13.530 --> 01:01:16.730
Three weeks ago, she calls me.

01:01:16.730 --> 01:01:17.730
She's scared.

01:01:17.730 --> 01:01:18.720
She's nervous.

01:01:18.720 --> 01:01:21.980
She said she'd found something that she shouldn't have found.

01:01:21.980 --> 01:01:28.070
She kept going on about buying a prepaid phone so it couldn't be traced back to her.

01:01:30.090 --> 01:01:33.410
I told her to go to your superior officer.

01:01:33.410 --> 01:01:35.640
Staff Sergeant Cullen.

01:01:35.640 --> 01:01:39.750
- What did she find?

01:01:39.750 --> 01:01:46.670
- Whatever she found, got her killed.

01:01:46.670 --> 01:01:48.550
- He's having a lot of feelings right now,

01:01:48.550 --> 01:01:49.870
understandably.

01:01:49.870 --> 01:01:51.390
I believe it's his explanations.

01:01:51.390 --> 01:01:52.270
- Me too.

01:01:52.270 --> 01:01:53.830
I don't know where to go from here.

01:01:53.830 --> 01:01:57.190
We have no evidence linking Sam Park to Kurt's murder,

01:01:57.190 --> 01:01:59.410
and I can't see him killing his own daughter.

01:01:59.410 --> 01:02:00.000
And now,

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:02.720
- I have to turn Cheryl Park's body over to the MP's.

01:02:02.720 --> 01:02:04.680
The case is no longer ours to pursue.

01:02:04.680 --> 01:02:06.340
- Monty, you gotta stall 'em.

01:02:06.340 --> 01:02:08.020
There's something that's going on over that base,

01:02:08.020 --> 01:02:08.920
and we have to find out what

01:02:08.920 --> 01:02:10.360
before they sweep it all under the rug.

01:02:10.360 --> 01:02:11.640
- Okay, let's go over this again.

01:02:11.640 --> 01:02:14.700
So we have a private who works at a distribution center.

01:02:14.700 --> 01:02:17.100
She tells her father she found something she shouldn't have.

01:02:17.100 --> 01:02:18.820
- Yeah, she trusted Kurt enough to send him a photo.

01:02:18.820 --> 01:02:21.180
- Which somehow is the proof of what she found.

01:02:21.180 --> 01:02:23.160
It just looks like a photo she took at work.

01:02:23.160 --> 01:02:25.320
- I will have forensics do a full workup on the photo.

01:02:25.320 --> 01:02:28.750
Maybe there's more to it than meets the eye.

01:02:28.750 --> 01:02:30.000
- Jonas, thanks for canceling the record.

01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:32.840
I just wasn't in the mood for something fancy tonight.

01:02:32.840 --> 01:02:34.800
I know you're worried about Fincher.

01:02:34.800 --> 01:02:37.220
There's just not much I can do for him.

01:02:37.220 --> 01:02:39.540
Hayley, you're doing a lot just by being there for him.

01:02:39.540 --> 01:02:47.000
Ugh, sorry about that.

01:02:47.000 --> 01:02:48.380
I do have some good news.

01:02:48.380 --> 01:02:51.540
The hospital has raised, ready?

01:02:51.540 --> 01:02:56.060
$25,000 from the calendar, and that is just so far.

01:02:56.060 --> 01:02:57.720
That's incredible.

01:03:00.280 --> 01:03:03.280
So, I wanted to thank you for convincing me to do it.

01:03:03.280 --> 01:03:05.780
Well, the hospital getting the support it needs is thanks enough.

01:03:05.780 --> 01:03:08.340
I'm sorry, I'll just turn this off.

01:03:08.340 --> 01:03:10.830
You can't turn it off. What if work needs you?

01:03:10.830 --> 01:03:11.810
Oh, right.

01:03:11.810 --> 01:03:13.870
What's going on?

01:03:13.870 --> 01:03:20.120
It's nothing, I just... I keep getting calls from the local news asking for an interview.

01:03:20.120 --> 01:03:21.800
Because of the calendar?

01:03:21.800 --> 01:03:24.300
I keep telling them to interview Megan, but they won't stop calling.

01:03:24.300 --> 01:03:27.240
Hi, um, can I take a photo with you?

01:03:27.240 --> 01:03:28.470
Oh, I don't...

01:03:28.470 --> 01:03:30.000
We're kind of having a private dinner.

01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:37.490
- No, no, of course, it'll only take a second.

01:03:37.490 --> 01:03:40.590
- Jonas, hi.

01:03:40.590 --> 01:03:41.810
- There you go.

01:03:41.810 --> 01:03:44.180
- Thank you.

01:03:44.180 --> 01:03:46.210
- Wow, it's incredible.

01:03:46.210 --> 01:03:49.900
She interrupts our dinner and doesn't even apologize.

01:03:49.900 --> 01:03:51.370
- Hm?

01:03:51.370 --> 01:03:52.390
- I am so sorry.

01:03:52.390 --> 01:03:56.620
- Let's just eat.

01:03:56.620 --> 01:04:00.000
So we got lucky, the burner had GPS and the location service

01:04:00.000 --> 01:04:01.550
services weren't turned off.

01:04:01.550 --> 01:04:04.010
We have a record of everywhere that Cheryl went

01:04:04.010 --> 01:04:05.230
on the day that she died.

01:04:05.230 --> 01:04:06.100
- We're ready.

01:04:06.100 --> 01:04:08.880
- Right, she started in Albany on base, I presume.

01:04:08.880 --> 01:04:10.860
And then she drove all the way here to Atlanta,

01:04:10.860 --> 01:04:13.520
arriving around 5:00 p.m.

01:04:13.520 --> 01:04:15.080
- So she drove straight through?

01:04:15.080 --> 01:04:16.320
- Yeah, it looks that way.

01:04:16.320 --> 01:04:19.070
And she hung out in a coffee shop for a while.

01:04:19.070 --> 01:04:20.390
She called Kurt several times,

01:04:20.390 --> 01:04:22.320
but he never answered any of them.

01:04:22.320 --> 01:04:23.710
- I wonder why.

01:04:23.710 --> 01:04:27.250
- Then at 8:00 p.m. she went to the park.

01:04:27.250 --> 01:04:28.290
- Where she was killed.

01:04:28.290 --> 01:04:29.500
Did you find the car?

01:04:29.500 --> 01:04:30.000
- No.

01:04:30.350 --> 01:04:34.030
the killer wanted her to disappear i wouldn't be surprised if it was sold to a chop shop and its

01:04:34.030 --> 01:04:40.610
parts spread all over the country by now so what now probably nothing the brass upstairs made me

01:04:40.610 --> 01:04:46.540
called marines this morning the mps are coming by later today to pick up the body and the files

01:04:46.540 --> 01:04:51.560
so soon i don't know how much further we could have gotten without access to kurt's files anyway

01:04:51.560 --> 01:04:59.830
i'm really sorry you guys okay you need to eat everything looks better on a full stomach

01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:02.190
- Sounds like a plan.

01:05:02.190 --> 01:05:03.890
- We'd like to place an order.

01:05:03.890 --> 01:05:05.310
- You two can read, correct?

01:05:05.310 --> 01:05:08.130
See, sorry, we're on a break.

01:05:08.130 --> 01:05:09.770
- Uh, did George sell the truck?

01:05:09.770 --> 01:05:11.150
- He's having his tonsils removed.

01:05:11.150 --> 01:05:13.550
I'm filling in right after my break.

01:05:13.550 --> 01:05:16.740
- Well, could you do one order really, really fast, please?

01:05:16.740 --> 01:05:17.940
- You're not gonna give up, are you?

01:05:17.940 --> 01:05:20.540
Okay, what do you want, will it be?

01:05:20.540 --> 01:05:21.490
- What do you recommend?

01:05:21.490 --> 01:05:23.030
- Okay, read off the menu.

01:05:23.030 --> 01:05:25.090
I recommend you order from there.

01:05:25.090 --> 01:05:27.410
You know what, let me make it easy for you two.

01:05:27.410 --> 01:05:29.890
How about pulled pork, right?

01:05:30.000 --> 01:05:30.880
A plain pig.

01:05:31.200 --> 01:05:32.500
It's meat on a bun.

01:05:32.580 --> 01:05:33.260
People love it.

01:05:34.230 --> 01:05:36.670
Uh, you know, I'm going to go with the bacon burger.

01:05:37.010 --> 01:05:37.590
Out of bacon.

01:05:38.740 --> 01:05:39.820
Chili cheese dog?

01:05:40.110 --> 01:05:40.820
Out of chili.

01:05:41.020 --> 01:05:41.580
Out of cheese.

01:05:41.820 --> 01:05:42.420
Out of dog.

01:05:43.810 --> 01:05:44.830
Sorry.

01:05:45.170 --> 01:05:45.450
You know what?

01:05:45.470 --> 01:05:46.950
We'll just take two of whatever you want to give us.

01:05:47.070 --> 01:05:48.550
Two plain pigs.

01:05:48.750 --> 01:05:49.450
You'll love it.

01:05:49.510 --> 01:05:49.810
There you go.

01:05:50.180 --> 01:05:50.890
Thank you.

01:05:50.990 --> 01:05:51.690
I'll keep the tip.

01:05:51.870 --> 01:05:52.430
There you go.

01:05:52.650 --> 01:05:52.990
Bye-bye.

01:05:57.380 --> 01:05:57.920
Looks edible.

01:05:58.320 --> 01:06:00.000
It's not exactly a re-endorsement.

01:06:01.660 --> 01:06:02.660
Hot sauce for your thoughts?

01:06:03.360 --> 01:06:04.530
I don't know, Haley.

01:06:05.170 --> 01:06:08.730
Just as we start getting close, the Marines show up and take everything away again.

01:06:09.130 --> 01:06:10.260
You're not giving up, are you?

01:06:10.560 --> 01:06:11.630
No, no, no.

01:06:11.730 --> 01:06:13.750
I just don't know where to go from here.

01:06:14.580 --> 01:06:16.340
Okay, let's look at what we might be missing.

01:06:16.760 --> 01:06:20.740
So, is there any way to connect Cheryl to Elisa Greystone?

01:06:20.820 --> 01:06:22.140
We already know she had something to hide.

01:06:22.220 --> 01:06:23.360
Maybe it's bigger than we expected.

01:06:23.700 --> 01:06:24.760
She's dating Lieutenant Young.

01:06:25.410 --> 01:06:28.450
He can influence who gets contracts and Barry reports if he wants to.

01:06:28.940 --> 01:06:30.000
Do you think he would...

01:06:30.030 --> 01:06:32.850
killed two people to keep his girlfriend's business afloat?

01:06:32.850 --> 01:06:36.700
People have killed for a lot less.

01:06:36.700 --> 01:06:39.700
Sergeant Nesbitt?

01:06:39.700 --> 01:06:40.550
Miss Dean?

01:06:40.550 --> 01:06:42.510
Here to take over the Sheryl Park case, I assume?

01:06:42.510 --> 01:06:45.360
No, actually, I'm here to work on it together.

01:06:45.360 --> 01:06:46.640
And for the record, if it were up to me,

01:06:46.640 --> 01:06:48.310
I would have been working with you all along.

01:06:48.310 --> 01:06:49.230
I appreciate that.

01:06:49.230 --> 01:06:51.470
When Detective Montgomery called me to fill me in

01:06:51.470 --> 01:06:53.590
about Private Park, I remembered an incident

01:06:53.590 --> 01:06:55.270
that happened the day she went AWOL.

01:06:55.270 --> 01:06:57.930
You mean when she was murdered?

01:06:57.930 --> 01:07:00.000
Here's Sheryl leaving the base at one

01:07:00.000 --> 01:07:03.840
p.m. on Thursday the 11th. It's nothing unusual. She could have been going out

01:07:03.840 --> 01:07:12.890
base for lunch. Then it's Kayla. That does not look like a pleasant

01:07:12.890 --> 01:07:30.000
conversation. She hasn't been honest with us. What else has she had

01:07:30.000 --> 01:07:32.620
-But she doesn't fit the evidence.

01:07:32.620 --> 01:07:36.320
-She has motive, Fincher. Strong motive.

01:07:36.320 --> 01:07:43.250
-We have video footage of you confronting Cheryl

01:07:43.250 --> 01:07:45.950
at the Marine base, so you do know her.

01:07:45.950 --> 01:07:50.430
-No. No, I don't.

01:07:50.430 --> 01:07:54.140
-Why did you suspect that she was seeing your husband?

01:07:54.140 --> 01:07:56.990
-I followed him a couple of weeks ago.

01:07:56.990 --> 01:07:59.600
He went to a hotel.

01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:07.400
saw him meet that woman in the lobby and you assumed the worst wouldn't you did you say anything

01:08:07.400 --> 01:08:14.380
to anyone about what you suspected i asked kurt i told him i saw him with another woman all he

01:08:14.380 --> 01:08:23.530
said was it was better for me not to know i mean what kind of answer was that all he said was it

01:08:23.530 --> 01:08:30.000
was better for me not to know what kind of answer was that so you thought that you would go to private

01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:36.330
park and get your answers. Walk me through what happened that day. You went to base? I waited at

01:08:36.330 --> 01:08:45.370
the gate for hours and I was about to give up when I saw her. You confronted her. Did she confirm

01:08:45.370 --> 01:08:50.290
your suspicions? She kept telling me to mind my own business if I knew what was best for me.

01:08:50.930 --> 01:08:55.250
And that made you angry? Of course it made me angry. So angry that you followed her all the

01:08:55.250 --> 01:09:00.000
way back to Atlanta that same day? No. And then maybe you heard

01:09:00.000 --> 01:09:03.650
Or maybe you were at home arguing with him when she called.

01:09:03.650 --> 01:09:06.210
You confronted her again. You hit her.

01:09:06.210 --> 01:09:08.460
Then you dragged her to the park, and you shot her.

01:09:08.460 --> 01:09:10.160
-No, you're wrong. -And then maybe

01:09:10.160 --> 01:09:12.610
Kurt found out that she didn't show up for work.

01:09:12.610 --> 01:09:15.110
Maybe someone on the base told him that you were there.

01:09:15.110 --> 01:09:18.320
You got into an argument, and you hit him, too.

01:09:18.320 --> 01:09:20.710
Enough to make him weak, and then maybe

01:09:20.710 --> 01:09:23.420
you told him you were taking him to the hospital.

01:09:23.420 --> 01:09:27.130
Instead, you took him to the park.

01:09:27.130 --> 01:09:30.000
-No. No, I could never hurt him.

01:09:31.020 --> 01:09:32.120
Even though we hurt you.

01:09:38.600 --> 01:09:49.000
He's going to take that as a confession.

01:09:49.940 --> 01:09:50.980
Well, she feels guilt.

01:09:51.640 --> 01:09:54.180
Not much as obvious, but she also feels backed into a corner.

01:09:55.270 --> 01:09:56.550
Do you think she did it?

01:09:59.030 --> 01:09:59.740
I don't know, Fincher.

01:10:05.950 --> 01:10:09.290
But now he has confirmation that his daughter was murdered.

01:10:09.290 --> 01:10:11.290
His threats might not be so idle.

01:10:11.290 --> 01:10:12.560
Haley, it's nice to see you here.

01:10:12.560 --> 01:10:13.560
Am I interrupting?

01:10:13.560 --> 01:10:16.100
No, I'm pretty much done.

01:10:16.100 --> 01:10:19.900
I don't want to press charges on Mr. Park for the threatening note.

01:10:19.900 --> 01:10:21.910
And I'm worried that he may escalate.

01:10:21.910 --> 01:10:22.910
What do you think, Haley?

01:10:22.910 --> 01:10:24.730
With only a threatening note to prosecute,

01:10:24.730 --> 01:10:26.680
I'm worried that he may escalate.

01:10:26.680 --> 01:10:27.940
What do you think, Haley?

01:10:27.940 --> 01:10:30.000
With only a threatening note to prosecute,

01:10:30.000 --> 01:10:32.300
a grieving military father could capture

01:10:32.300 --> 01:10:34.340
public sentiment and you'd lose the case.

01:10:34.340 --> 01:10:37.770
- As usual, your intuition is spot on.

01:10:37.770 --> 01:10:40.950
It's a trait I wish I could inject into all my ADAs.

01:10:40.950 --> 01:10:43.110
It's like old times, Haley.

01:10:43.110 --> 01:10:46.360
- So where's Fincher?

01:10:46.360 --> 01:10:50.160
- With Megan, under strict orders to eat and sleep.

01:10:50.160 --> 01:10:53.520
- It's hard to lose a friend to needless violence.

01:10:53.520 --> 01:10:57.390
- Haley, I'm sorry, I didn't mean it.

01:10:57.390 --> 01:10:59.730
- Oh, it's okay, Monty, really.

01:11:00.730 --> 01:11:06.200
i just feel like we're missing something forensics didn't find anything unusual it hadn't been

01:11:06.200 --> 01:11:11.620
doctored so no idea where it was taken there was no geographic tag they only said albany we already

01:11:11.620 --> 01:11:20.880
figured it was taken on base so not much help can i keep this yes we have plenty when you said

01:11:20.880 --> 01:11:25.200
you'd send over clayton morrell's case file i didn't expect you to do it in person well you know

01:11:25.200 --> 01:11:30.000
i'm a fan of the personal touch actually i'm really glad you called i was driving myself crazy trying to find

01:11:30.000 --> 01:11:35.460
the hidden meaning of this photo so any distraction is welcome can I get you some tea yes but I can't

01:11:35.460 --> 01:11:45.010
stay long your house is so lovely it suits you perfectly thanks and then there was the guy who

01:11:45.010 --> 01:11:50.330
used to dress like a lion I hope he got the help he needed what he needed was a lawyer who wouldn't

01:11:50.330 --> 01:11:56.490
let him wear his lion mask into court oh my gosh we've had some crazy cases over the years

01:11:56.490 --> 01:11:59.760
they're still going on and the sad ones too

01:12:01.050 --> 01:12:05.470
I am not looking forward to Clayton Morrell's parole hearing next month.

01:12:05.470 --> 01:12:08.890
But knowing that you're going to testify to is a big relief.

01:12:08.890 --> 01:12:11.600
Whatever I can do to help.

01:12:11.600 --> 01:12:17.000
You know, Haley, I have given my entire career to the DA's office.

01:12:17.000 --> 01:12:20.200
I could have gone private or corporate, I had the offers.

01:12:20.200 --> 01:12:22.870
Why didn't you?

01:12:22.870 --> 01:12:29.250
Because I felt like I'd be letting down the innocents who needed people like us to get them the justice they deserve.

01:12:30.000 --> 01:12:32.270
But now I'm starting to feel like none of it mattered.

01:12:32.270 --> 01:12:34.690
Paulina, you know that's not true.

01:12:34.690 --> 01:12:38.200
One man coming up for parole does not erase your entire career.

01:12:38.200 --> 01:12:41.410
I know.

01:12:41.410 --> 01:12:46.550
I should really get going because I have a mountain of paperwork to get through tonight.

01:12:46.550 --> 01:12:49.830
That is one thing I do not miss, the paperwork.

01:12:49.830 --> 01:12:50.780
Oh.

01:12:50.780 --> 01:12:53.000
So there are things you do miss.

01:12:53.000 --> 01:12:55.410
You are one of those things.

01:12:55.410 --> 01:12:57.440
Thanks for the girl time.

01:12:57.440 --> 01:13:00.000
Let me know when you have a chance to get

01:13:00.000 --> 01:13:11.220
through this case file will do oh pretty girl it's another victim who needs your help sadly yes

01:13:12.270 --> 01:13:17.280
well if there's anyone who can help her it's you i'm gonna let myself out

01:13:37.130 --> 01:13:39.320
- Hey, you've reached Fincher, give me a message.

01:13:39.320 --> 01:13:41.120
- Hey Finch, it's Hayley.

01:13:41.120 --> 01:13:42.880
I'm looking at this picture of Private Park

01:13:42.880 --> 01:13:44.560
and I swear I've seen that creep before.

01:13:44.560 --> 01:13:45.300
Call me back.

01:14:05.400 --> 01:14:06.380
Hey.

01:14:06.380 --> 01:14:07.390
Hey Haley.

01:14:07.390 --> 01:14:09.220
Sorry I didn't listen to your voicemail.

01:14:09.220 --> 01:14:11.220
I was thinking about the crates in the background of that photo.

01:14:11.220 --> 01:14:14.080
Yeah, I think it's the proof Private Park was talking about.

01:14:14.080 --> 01:14:17.390
I'm looking at them right now.

01:14:17.390 --> 01:14:18.390
I'm at Houston Industries.

01:14:18.390 --> 01:14:21.630
Wait, you're at Houston's warehouse right now?

01:14:21.630 --> 01:14:23.610
Haley, do you know what's in those crates?

01:14:23.610 --> 01:14:26.080
I'm about to find out.

01:14:31.820 --> 01:14:35.000
- It says to be destroyed.

01:14:35.000 --> 01:14:36.980
- Hayley, the only thing the military sends home

01:14:36.980 --> 01:14:38.480
to be destroyed are guns.

01:14:38.480 --> 01:14:41.910
That's what must be in those crates.

01:14:41.910 --> 01:14:43.390
Private Park must have figured out the shipping

